          "quote": "This is attributed to a dynamic strain ageing (DSA) phenomenon increasing strengths by obstacles to the movement of dislocations during strain. This DSA phenomenon has been well known to be generated at specific temperature ranges for solid solution alloys like austenitic stainless steels [17]. It is thus believed that the DSA was generated at this temperature range for Alloy 617 which is a solid solution alloy.",
